  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Morning Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    29 July 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good morning Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,222.94/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SHEMA</td>\n                <td>₦1,216.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,216.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,243.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.50</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,216.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AITEO</td>\n                <td>₦1,216.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>A.Y.M SHAFA</td>\n                <td>₦1,243.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>EMADEB</td>\n                <td>₦1,218.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,608.75/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SAHARA</td>\n                <td>₦1,620.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TMDK</td>\n                <td>₦1,620.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,605.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,605.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,605.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,605.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,610.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    DAPPMAN Alleges Selective Fuel Import Licence Allocations, Seeks Reps' Intervention\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Depot and Petroleum Products Marketers Association of Nigeria (DAPPMAN) has accused the Nigerian Midstream and Downstream Petroleum Regulatory Authority of repeatedly allocating fuel import licences to the same group of marketers. The allegation was made on Tuesday during an interactive session organised by the House Committee on Petroleum Resources (Downstream)\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dappman-alleges-selective-fuel-import-licence-allocations-seeks-reps-intervention\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    JUST IN: Brent Crude Jumps 4% to $87 After Iran strikes U.S Military\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was trading at $87.59 per barrel, up 4.16 per cent. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) stood at $82.53 per barrel,. representing a 4.13 per cent gain. The latest rally comes barely 24 hours after oil prices retreated.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/just-in-brent-crude-jumps-4-to-87-after-iran-strikes-us-military\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Private Depots Undercut Dangote as Diesel Prices Fall to ₦1,600/Litre\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Private petroleum depot owners in Lagos have intensified competition in Nigeria's diesel market after slashing Automotive Gas Oil (AGO) prices below Dangote Refinery's ex-depot rate. The development means marketers sourcing diesel from these private depots now enjoy a price advantage of between ⁦40 and ₦50 per litre.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/private-depots-undercut-dangote-as-diesel-prices-fall-to-1600litre\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Again, Oil Prices Sink Nearly 7% as U.S.-Iran Diplomacy Gains Momentum\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude traded at $82.80 per barrel , down 6.29 percent , while West Texas Intermediate (WTI) fell 5.58 percent to $78.00 per barrel. The latest losses came as investors responded positively to signs that Washington and Tehran could be moving closer to renewed negotiations.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/again-oil-prices-sink-nearly-7-as-us-iran-diplomacy-gains-momentum\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Petroleumprice.ng Rolls Out 2026 Awards Timeline\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The 2026 Petroleumprice.ng Awards will celebrate excellence, innovation and outstanding contributions across Nigeria's downstream petroleum industry. The nomination process will be conducted entirely online through a dedicated digital platform. Participation is free, and each individual will be permitted to submit only one nomination throughout the exercise to ensure fairness and credibility.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/petroleumpriceng-rolls-out-2026-awards-timeline\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
